  "description": "GUPNIS crystallizes in the rhombohedral crystal system with space group R -3 c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C34 H80 Eu5 Mn5 N8 O48 2+,2(N1 O3 1-),12(H2 O1),2(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 9 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu4 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Mn6 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn7 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn9 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Eu5 (Eu) has 9 O neighbors; Eu6 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Mn4 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn5 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 24 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.139-3.804 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 84.23-130.13°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Mn5III Eu5III (μ4-O)4 (μ2-OH)2 (OAc)8 (OCH3)2 (ampdH)4 (NO3)4 (H2O)4](NO3)2·12H2O·2MeOH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ2-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
